{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8231814",
      "title": "Using useEffect for Syncing With Browser APIs",
      "sourceHash": "b86fe94218915c387aeff8d861a083e6ce90edf6b8f15a25a799d4196b2e6392",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.69,
          "end": 4.05,
          "en": "So how can we use useEffect to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.05,
          "end": 7.41,
          "en": "that depending on the value of this open prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.41,
          "end": 11.343,
          "en": "this dialog here is shown or closed?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.6,
          "end": 17.6,
          "en": "Well, we could first try it without useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.67,
          "end": 20.22,
          "en": "because here in the modal component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.22,
          "end": 22.32,
          "en": "we can, of course, add a if check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.32,
          "end": 25.26,
          "en": "and check if open is truthy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.26,
          "end": 28.47,
          "en": "And if that's the case, we use the dialog ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.47,
          "end": 33.363,
          "en": "to call showModal like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.16,
          "end": 38.91,
          "en": "Else if it's not truthy, it's faulty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.91,
          "end": 42.633,
          "en": "So in that case, we call close to close it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 44.25,
          "end": 46.23,
          "en": "But if we try to run this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.23,
          "end": 49.11,
          "en": "if we save it and we go back and we reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.11,
          "end": 52.23,
          "en": "that's important, we'll get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.23,
          "end": 55.92,
          "en": "We'll get an error that we in the end failed to call close",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.92,
          "end": 57.9,
          "en": "which is what we try to do initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.9,
          "end": 61.27,
          "en": "because initially open is false in the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.64,
          "end": 66.57,
          "en": "so that we try to call close on undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 66.57,
          "end": 68.37,
          "en": "And the problem here, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.37,
          "end": 71.64,
          "en": "is that we're calling these methods here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 71.64,
          "end": 73.35,
          "en": "showModal and close,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.35,
          "end": 76.773,
          "en": "right inside of this component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.09,
          "end": 80.1,
          "en": "And we're using the dialog ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.1,
          "end": 82.92,
          "en": "to interact with that dialog.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.92,
          "end": 87.06,
          "en": "But the first time this component function executes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.06,
          "end": 89.73,
          "en": "this ref will not be set yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.73,
          "end": 91.71000000000001,
          "en": "It will not be connected yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.71000000000001,
          "end": 95.10300000000001,
          "en": "because this JSX code hasn't executed yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.09,
          "end": 99.9,
          "en": "So this connection between a ref and dialog element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.9,
          "end": 101.72999999999999,
          "en": "hasn't been established yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.72999999999999,
          "end": 105.47999999999999,
          "en": "and therefore calling close fails because initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.47999999999999,
          "end": 107.85300000000001,
          "en": "this ref is undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.592,
          "end": 113.61699999999999,
          "en": "And that's another scenario where you wanna use useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 114.63,
          "end": 119.63,
          "en": "because useEffect can help you synchronize prop values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 120,
          "end": 125,
          "en": "or state values to DOM APIs like this dialog",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 125.197,
          "end": 130.197,
          "en": "showModal method or a close method because as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 130.23,
          "end": 133.8,
          "en": "the effect function you define with useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 133.8,
          "end": 138.78,
          "en": "will be executed right after the component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 138.78,
          "end": 142.38,
          "en": "And since it executes after the component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 142.38,
          "end": 145.56,
          "en": "and not before it or at the same time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 145.56,
          "end": 148.74,
          "en": "this connection between the ref and the dialog",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 148.74,
          "end": 151.473,
          "en": "will be established at this point of time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 153.6,
          "end": 156.84,
          "en": "And we can indeed think of that code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 156.84,
          "end": 159.87,
          "en": "as kind of a side effect as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 159.87,
          "end": 162.69,
          "en": "because whilst calling these methods here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 162.69,
          "end": 165.99,
          "en": "will indeed have an impact on the UI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 165.99,
          "end": 170.49,
          "en": "it does not have a direct impact on this JSX code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 170.49,
          "end": 173.16,
          "en": "So it's again not directly related",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 173.16,
          "end": 175.173,
          "en": "to this component render cycle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 176.34,
          "end": 179.64,
          "en": "So therefore here we should now also useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 179.64,
          "end": 184.26,
          "en": "now not to avoid an infinite loop with some side effect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 184.26,
          "end": 187.41,
          "en": "but to synchronize some value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 187.41,
          "end": 189.54,
          "en": "the open prop in this case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 189.54,
          "end": 193.533,
          "en": "to a DOM API or to a certain behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 195.33,
          "end": 197.85,
          "en": "So for that, we can call useEffect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 197.85,
          "end": 201.96,
          "en": "pass our effect function to it and our dependency array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 201.96,
          "end": 206.013,
          "en": "and then we can move this code here into useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 208.07999999999998,
          "end": 212.553,
          "en": "And now you can already see that I'm getting a warning here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 213.39,
          "end": 216.69,
          "en": "You can tell by the yellow squiggly lines here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 216.69,
          "end": 218.25,
          "en": "I'm getting a warning here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 218.25,
          "end": 220.95,
          "en": "because I haven't added all the dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 220.95,
          "end": 223.86,
          "en": "that are required by this effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 223.86,
          "end": 225.573,
          "en": "to this dependencies array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 226.8,
          "end": 228.27,
          "en": "Now in the app component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 228.27,
          "end": 231,
          "en": "it was fine to have an empty array here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 231,
          "end": 233.34,
          "en": "because this effect code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 233.34,
          "end": 236.163,
          "en": "in the end had no extra dependencies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 237.24,
          "end": 240.78,
          "en": "but this code here has dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 240.78,
          "end": 244.02,
          "en": "And therefore, it's, of course, important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 244.02,
          "end": 248.043,
          "en": "what exactly are such effect dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}